<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Médéa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Médéa is a city in the Tell <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, about 80 km south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. From the 16th century it was the seat of the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">Beylik</a> of Titteri, a market town for grain, livestock and wool. French forces fought for it repeatedly against Abdelkader before taking it in 1840. It is now the capital of Médéa province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/medea.jpg" alt="Médéa" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: habib kaki · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%A9d%C3%A9a_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
